# Inventory invariants (mandatory)

## Ledger and caches
- `InventoryMovement` is the inventory ledger; as-of stock and movement reports read it.
- `ItemWarehouseBalance` (quantity, reserved, average cost), `ItemQuantity` (per location), `Item.averageCost` and `ItemCostHistory` are caches and history. Never update them directly as a shortcut; repairs go through `inventoryCostingService.recalculateItemCostHistory`.

## Costing
- Moving weighted average. Inbound updates the average; outbound is valued at the current average.
- Use `inventoryCostingService.applyInboundMovement`, `applyOutboundMovement`, `reverseInboundInTx`; they call `stockMovementService.postMovementInTx`.
- Known gaps, do not copy: POS and manufacturing issues post movements without the costing service; purchase-invoice unpost repairs cost after its transaction (audit M-09).

## Locking and posting
- Stock changes go through `lockStockRowsInTx` / `postMovementInTx` / `adjustStockInTx` (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`, atomic quantity increment). Sort lines with `sortForStockLocking` before locking. Negative-stock checks run after the locks, inside the transaction.
- Claim the document first inside the posting transaction with `claimDocumentPost` (and `claimDocumentUnpost` for unpost), like receipts, issues, stocktaking, assembly and disassembly. Transfers and adjustments currently lack this (audit H-01); new document types must not.
- Stock, cost, GL entry and party effects of one document post in one transaction (reference: `invoicePostingOrchestrator.post`, `postTransfer` both legs at the outbound unit cost).

## Reversal
- Unpost / cancel must reverse exactly the original effects: same movements, quantities and costs, in the same transaction.

## Numbers and GL keys
- Stock document serials are client-entered and not unique; the stock GL `activeSourceKey` uses them (audit M-03). Do not build new source keys from non-unique values.

## Heavy work
- Catalog-wide recalculation (fix average cost) holds stock locks per item; run it as a background job, not inside a normal request, when adding or changing such tools.
